  (footprint "wl-sync:BNC_Dual_RA_Isolated" 
    (layer "F.Cu") 
    (uuid "55b6ad6d-5837-4e21-96ef-39f6784ff59e") 
    (at 139.0 225.55 180.0) 
    (descr "Dual-port 50 ohm BNC jack, RIGHT ANGLE, each port's shell isolated from the OTHER port's (NOT from the panel: the threaded bushing is the shell, so it needs an insulated panel hole). Amphenol RF 031-6575, customer outline drawing 31-6575 rev A (2013-04-18). Ports stacked vertically at 16.0mm; panel holes 12.83mm at the same pitch, 1/2-28 UNEF. PCB pattern: 4 x 0.89mm signal (pad 1 = port A centre, 2 = port A shell, 3 = port B centre, 4 = port B shell) and 2 x 2.01mm plated, unnumbered POST-MOUNT holes (the sibling drawing 31-6576 rev B calls them that; they are the mounting hooks, not ground terminals). Body 14.4 x 36.2mm. Replaces BNC_PanelMountable_Vertical, whose axis was perpendicular to the board (F6). NOT KiCad's own BNC_Win_364A2x95_Horizontal, which commons both shells (it models a FRONT-isolated part) and draws a different manufacturer's body. PIN MAP READ FROM THE DRAWINGS (R11, 2026-11-21): port A (pads 1, 2) is the UPPER port, 23 mm above the board, and port B (pads 3, 4) the LOWER, 7 mm above it -- 31-6576 rev B Detail A labels pad 1's hole HIGH PORT SIGNAL and pad 3's LOW PORT SIGNAL, and 31-6575 rev A's rear and side views draw the same. Not checked against a part: continuity from each port's centre to its pad is a first-box bring-up check.") 
    (tags "connector BNC coaxial dual right-angle isolated panel Amphenol 031-6575") 
    (property "Reference" "J48" 
      (at 0 2.35 0.0) 
      (layer "F.SilkS") 
      (uuid "dac3b776-1937-4225-b82e-fe3e6869edea") 
